  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>460</x>
      <y>1730</y>
      <w>310</w>
      <h>120</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Adapter pattern*
Target: LLMClient, RecipeSource
Adapters: GeminiClient, OllamaClient,
MealDBRecipeSource
Adaptees: the Gemini SDK, the Ollama
HTTP API, the TheMealDB HTTP API
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>380</x>
      <y>1380</y>
      <w>270</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>*Factory Method pattern*
Creator: LLMClientFactory
Factory method: create_client()
Product: LLMClient
Concrete products: GeminiClient,
OllamaClient, chosen by
Config.llm_provider
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2070</x>
      <y>230</y>
      <w>300</w>
      <h>90</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>The free key searches one ingredient
at a time, so search_by_ingredients()
runs one request per ingredient and
merges the results.
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>880</x>
      <y>240</y>
      <w>350</w>
      <h>70</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Each Postgres...Repository implements every
method of its interface using SQL (methods
not repeated to keep the diagram readable).
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>60</x>
      <y>120</y>
      <w>350</w>
      <h>70</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>claim_if_unclaimed() is a single
conditional UPDATE, so when two members
claim the same item, only the first wins.
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
